! Floating-point diagnostic jb_af1c, routine F210 "STORE ROUNDED TEST
! ROUTINE", sub-tests A1-A2 (docs/jb_af1c_floating-point.pdf p.110,
! octal 015775.00-016014.00, where F210A3 begins).
!
! The first block since F204 that is NOT a pure transcription: SRD
! (STORE ROUNDED, opcode 0101110) decodes but has no execute arm, so
! this program is the diagnostic that drives writing one.
!
! What the manual says (Ref. Manual p.96, "Store Rounded"). Rounding
! adds one to the accumulator fraction AT BIT POSITION 60, giving a
! 96-bit sum and a possible overflow bit; the 48 low-order bits are
! discarded. Unnormalized, the 48 high-order bits go to storage bits
! 12-59 and the overflow bit does not enter storage but sets LC. The
! accumulator sign, as changed by the sign modifiers, goes to storage
! bit 60 and the accumulator flag bits to 61-63. The entire
! accumulator and its sign byte register remain UNCHANGED. In the XFP
! or XFN range the rounding is still performed but the exponent is not
! changed, normalization is suppressed, and a rounding overflow bit is
! simply lost.
!
! A1 and A2 are both the flagged case, and they are a clean first test
! because their arithmetic is unambiguous:
!
!   A1  DL(U) FPK26 (XFP, high fraction all ones) then C0011 drops
!       FK40's all-ones fraction into the low half, so the accumulator
!       fraction is 96 ones. Adding 1 at IBM 60 carries the whole way
!       out: the 96-bit sum is 2^47-1, its high 48 bits are zero, and
!       the overflow is lost. Expected result FK35 -- XFP, same
!       exponent, fraction ZERO.
!   A2  the same shape in the XFN range with FK25, expecting FPK59.
!
! Each then asks two questions: CT0110(BU,60) against ROS at offset 4,
! which covers word bits 4-63 -- exponent and fraction, skipping the
! sign and flags -- and BZB on ROS bit 60, the stored sign.
!
! A reading note on the printed comments. A1 says "EXP + +2047" where
! FPK26 decodes to XFP +1023, and A2 says "EXP + -1791" where FK25 is
! XFN -767. Both differ by exactly 1024: the listing writes the
! flagged exponent as its true out-of-range value, EF contributing the
! 1024. The constants are transcribed as printed; only the comments
! use that convention.
!
! ROS (022355) is the routine's scratch word, not a pool constant --
! SRD writes it and the checks read it back. It is reserved here the
! same way fp_arith_f204b.strap reserves it.
!
! Framework substitutes as everywhere else in this series: SERS (octal
! 1304) -> FAIL halt, SEN (octal 1310) -> scratch. Constants from the
! pools pp.176-177. PASS sits at 016014.00, where F210A3 begins.
!
! Instructions: B, DL(U), C0011, SRD(U), L, CT0110, SIC, BZB, BRGZ.
! verify_fp_arith_f210a1_2_listing.py checks every word bit-for-bit.

! -- SSIP framework substitutes --
        SLC, (8)1304.0
SERS    BEW, $
        SLC, (8)1310.0
SEN     DD(BU,64,8), 0

! -- the routine's scratch word --
        SLC, (8)22355.0
ROS     DD(BU,64,8), 0

! -- constants (pools pp.176-177) --
        SLC, (8)022037.0
FPK26   DD(BU,64,8), (8)1777577777777777777760
        SLC, (8)022100.0
FPK59   DD(BU,64,8), (8)1577600000000000000000
        SLC, (8)022173.0
FK25    DD(BU,64,8), (8)1577777777777777777760
        SLC, (8)022205.0
FK35    DD(BU,64,8), (8)1777400000000000000000
        SLC, (8)022212.0
FK40    DD(BU,64,8), (8)1777577777777777777770

! The listing prints no label at 015775.00 -- ENTRY is ours, needed
! only as the END operand. (SAP11 labels it in the listing, but that
! is the SSIP prologue's target, not this block's.)
! -- code (verbatim, at the listing's addresses) --
        SLC, (8)15775.0
ENTRY   B, $+.32                             ! F210A1: exponent of operand in XFP range
        DL(U), FPK26                         ! exp + +2047
        C0011(BU,48), FK40+.12, 20
        SRD(U), ROS
        L(BU), FK35
        CT0110(BU,60), ROS, 4                ! error if 1 not added in bit pos 60
        SIC, SEN
        BRGZ, SERS                           ! of accumulator
        BZB, ROS+.60, $+2.0                  ! check sign bit + 0
        SIC, SEN
        B, SERS
        B, $+.32                             ! F210A2: exponent of operand in XFN range
        DL(U), FK25                          ! exp + -1791
        C0011(BU,48), FK25+.12, 20
        SRD(U), ROS
        L(BU), FPK59
        CT0110(BU,60), ROS, 4
        SIC, SEN
        BRGZ, SERS
        BZB, ROS+.60, $+2.0
        SIC, SEN
        B, SERS
PASS    BEW, $                               ! 016014.00: where F210A3 begins
        END, ENTRY
